{"name":"Nomad","hex":"#a19986","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"nomad","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A member of a society or class who herd animals from pasture to pasture with no fixed home.","Synonym of wanderer: an itinerant person."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Synonym of nomadic."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/nomad"}],"entries":[{"title":"Nomad","blocks":[{"text":"Nomads are communities without fixed habitation who regularly move to and from areas. Such groups include hunter-gatherers, pastoral nomads, tinkers and trader nomads. In the twentieth century, the population of nomadic pastoral tribes slowly decreased, reaching an estimated 30–40 million nomads in the world as of 1995."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/5f/Encampment_of_Gypsies_with_Caravans.jpg/330px-Encampment_of_Gypsies_with_Caravans.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Nomad","wikidata":"Q128393"},{"title":"Nomad (Marvel Comics)","blocks":[{"text":"Nomad is the name of several fictional characters appearing in American comic books published by Marvel Comics. The Nomad name and costume were created by writer Steve Englehart and artist Sal Buscema as an alternate identity for the original Captain America, Steve Rogers, in Captain America #180."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/5/52/NomadLS-1.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Nomad_(Marvel_Comics)","wikidata":"Q3877909"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/04/Hungarian_Gypsy_Mother_and_Child_NGM-v31-p563.jpg/500px-Hungarian_Gypsy_Mother_and_Child_NGM-v31-p563.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/04/Hungarian_Gypsy_Mother_and_Child_NGM-v31-p56